<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάκος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό</span>, 
			Ion.
		 gen. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάκευς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					334
				</span></i>
			 (Cretan word acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				1096
			</span></i>):—<i>shield</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.478
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20.268
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.52
			</span></i>, etc.: it was concave, and hence sts. used as a vessel to
			hold liquid, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				540
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>shield, defence</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμός,
				ἄρρηκτον ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				190
			</span></i>. (Prob. cogn. with Skt. <i>tvác-</i> 'skin,
			hide'.)</div>
